        <strong>Location: </strong>
        </strong><span class="field-content">
      MDC Ozark Regional Office      </span></div><div class="views-field views-field-body"><div class="field-content">
      <p>This class is a series of 12 programs that meets once each month all year long, though you may join at any time. You will learn to use simple, but beautiful embroidery techniques to stitch quilt blocks of different species found in or around Missouri Streams. Including Raccoon, Red Eared Slider, Madtom, and Green Heron, At each class you will learn about one of the Species and it's history, habitat preferences, and its importance to Missouri. Classes will be held on either the first or second Tuesday of each month at 6:00 pm at the Ozark Regional Office Building in West Plains. At 551 Joe Jones Blvd West Plains MO, 65775. The thread colors needed that month, Block templates, and information cards will be provided at the class. 
</p>Please be aware that signing up means you will attempt to come to all 12 meetings.      </div></div></div>
    <div class="views-row"><div class="views-field [long]"><div class="field-content">
      <a href="https://mdc-event-web.s3licensing.com/Event/EventDetails/221250" target="_blank">Trapping: Trapping 101: Trap Prep</a>      </div></div><div class="views-field [long]"><strong class="views-label [long]">
        <strong>Registration period: </strong>
        </strong><span class="field-content">
      September 4 - October 5      </span></div><div class="views-field views-field-field-event-begin-date"><strong class="views-label views-label-field-event-begin-date">
        <strong>Date: </strong>
        </strong><span class="field-content">
      Tuesday, October 6, 2026 5:00 pm - Tuesday, October 6, 2026 7:00 pm      </span></div><div class="views-field views-field-views-conditional-field"><strong class="views-label views-label-views-conditional-field">
        <strong>Location: </strong>
        </strong><span class="field-content">
      Mingo National Wildlife Refuge Visitor Center      </span></div><div class="views-field views-field-body"><div class="field-content">
      <p>CURIOUS ABOUT TRAPPING?
</p><p>
</p><p>Ever wanted to learn how to harvest fur-bearers but didn’t know where to start? It all starts with the trap.
</p><p>
</p><p>This hands-on program is the first in a series of trapping programs brought to you by MDC, the Missouri Trappers Association, and local trapping experts. You’ll learn the basics of fur-bearer trap identification, traditional and modern preparation, and storage—the skills you need to get your gear ready before you hit the field.
</p><p>
</p><p>No experience? No problem. Whether you’re looking to build your outdoor skills, try something new, or have always been curious about trapping, this is a great place to start.
</p><p>
</p><p>Hands-on | No experience needed
</p><p>
</p><p>You don’t have to attend the entire series, but we recommend joining us for the full experience. Look for the other programs being held at Mingo NWR and Duck Creek CA.
</p><p>
</p>MINORS are allowed but must be accompanied by a registered adult.      </div></div></div>
    <div class="views-row"><div class="views-field [long]"><div class="field-content">
      <a href="https://mdc-event-web.s3licensing.com/Event/EventDetails/220846" target="_blank">Native Plants: Foraging Through the Seasons</a>      </div></div><div class="views-field [long]"><strong class="views-label [long]">
        <strong>Registration period: </strong>
        </strong><span class="field-content">
      August 21 - October 6      </span></div><div class="views-field views-field-field-event-begin-date"><strong class="views-label views-label-field-event-begin-date">
        <strong>Date: </strong>
        </strong><span class="field-content">
      Tuesday, October 6, 2026 6:00 pm - Tuesday, October 6, 2026 7:00 pm      </span></div><div class="views-field views-field-views-conditional-field"><strong class="views-label views-label-views-conditional-field">
        <strong>Location: </strong>
        </strong><span class="field-content">
      Springfield Conservation Nature Center      </span></div><div class="views-field views-field-body"><div class="field-content">
      Rachael West, owner and founder of Eating the Ozarks, explores how to forage responsibly and confidently throughout the year by focusing on seasonal cycles and the edible plants that emerge in each season. Learn to identify common, safe-to-harvest wild foods such as greens, berries, roots, and flowers, while gaining an understanding of plant life cycles, habitats, and ethical harvesting practices. West will also discuss ways to incorporate wild foods into everyday meals and build a deeper relationship with the land through observation and seasonal awareness. This presentation is perfect for beginners and those looking to deepen their connection to place. West is the owner, lead instructor, and founder of Eating the Ozarks, which offers foraging classes, wild-infused meals, and special event catering in southwest Missouri. Ages 12 and up. Registration required.      </div></div></div>

    
